          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "Ronald1995"
            },
            "body": "﻿## Verification on H20\n\n**Verified commit:** `50ffbf6b74a8b888e72b90ef07247093f80e2bb1` (this PR's head; it covers MiMo-V2 target)\n**Integration commit:** `c623df9e4bfe1133a3205b94e2d771ba43876ec7` (`attn-sink-integration` = #57797 + #57798 + #57801 + #57803 + #57804 + #57805 + #57806)\n### Environment\n\n- Cluster: H20 Slurm, node `vllm-h20-01`, 1x NVIDIA H20-3e (`--partition=h20 --gres=gpu:h20:1`)\n- Python: `$HOME/vllm-shared/prebuilt-venv/bin/python` (torch 2.13.0+cu130 + compiled vllm from the shared prebuilt baseline)\n- Pure-Python change, so the verified revision was overlaid onto the prebuilt package with `make-overlay.sh`; nothing was recompiled.\n\n### Results\n\n| Suite | Where | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `test_attention_sink_load_audit.py` (from #57806) | head node + GPU node | 39 passed |\n| `test_attn_sink_reload.py` (from #57797) | head node (CPU) | 18 passed, 2 skipped (CUDA-only) |\n| `test_attn_sink_reload.py` | H20 GPU | **20 passed** |\n| GPU end-to-end sink reload script | H20 GPU | **8/8 checks passed** |\n\nThe GPU script drives a real layerwise reload (`record_metadata_for_reloading` -> `initialize_layerwise_reload` -> `load_weights` -> `finalize_layerwise_reload`) on CUDA tensors and asserts the live update lands in the kernel tensor storage with the `-inf` padding tail re-established and the storage pointer unchanged:\n\n```text\nPASS  live update reaches kernel tensor\nPASS  live update re-establishes -inf padding\nPASS  kernel tensor storage is stable\nPASS  rank 1 live update loads its own heads\nALL GPU SINK CHECKS PASSED\n```\n\n### Pre-commit\n\n```text\npre-commit run --files <changed files>\npass1 rc=0 dirty=0\npass2 rc=0 dirty=0\n```\n\nNo hook rewrote a file. `run-precommit.sh` skips the `pip-compile` hooks because the sandbox cannot reach PyPI; no requirements file is touched here.\n\n### Not verified\n\n- No full-model checkpoint was loaded (no matching weights available), so this is loader/contract-level plus a real GPU reload, not a full-model accuracy run.\n- Single GPU; TP>1 was exercised in-process via distinct rank head ranges, not as a multi-process TP run.\r\n\n### What changed in this revision\n\nThe earlier revision reindented the whole tail of `load_weights` to drop an `else`, which also moved `maybe_remap_kv_scale_name` in front of the sink handling. That is unrelated to the sink write and changes behavior for a non-sink path. This revision keeps the sink branch self-contained: narrow, load through the current loader, `loaded_params.add`, `continue`. The diff is now the sink branch only.\r\n",
